# Reproducibility depends on byte-stable checkouts. Force LF everywhere so any clone,
# on any OS or global git config, checks out identical bytes (the review_sha256 and
# html_sha256 the gate/census pin are computed on LF content).
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
# held source exports are bytes, never normalised (their sha256 is the provenance)
outputs/handover/independent_search/** -text
outputs/handover/rob2_method/*.pdf -text
outputs/handover/glp1_comparators/*.xml -text
outputs/handover/glp1_comparators/*_epmc.json -text
# Served evidence bundle (2026-09-19): docs/<repo-root-relative ref> mirrors every input the review
# CERTIFICATE.json commits a digest to, so the refs resolve unmodified against the Pages site root.
# These are bytes, never normalised -- three held text exports carry CRLF, and a text=auto checkin
# would serve them off the digest the certificate commits to (a bundle that verifies as corrupt).
# scripts/build_bundle.py refuses to mirror a path whose `text` attribute is not unset.
docs/cache/** -text
docs/outputs/** -text
docs/protocols/** -text
docs/topics/** -text
docs/harness/** -text
docs/scripts/** -text
docs/acquisitions/** -text
evidence/held/** -text
# Frozen release archives (scripts/release_archive.py): the zip, its SHA256SUMS, RELEASE.json and README are bytes whose
# sha256 is the release identity -- never normalised.
docs/releases/** -text
